  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The underlying business is displaying solid organic expansion and a healthy acquisition appetite, broadening its communications and advisory service lines across the U.S. and Europe. Despite this operational momentum and inclusion in prominent Russell indices, the market has fixated on GAAP net losses driven by non-cash accounting items, creating a disconnect that several commentators describe as an overdone sell-off. The near-complete absence of balance-sheet leverage leaves the firm well insulated, yet the share-price reaction suggests sentiment has been weighed down by headline earnings optics rather than underlying organic growth.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is pursuing a deliberate buy-and-build strategy, executing accretive acquisitions that extend geographic and sector reach, while also attracting senior talent. The dual U.S. listing and index inclusion are being leveraged to raise the company’s profile. Management has viewed the stock weakness as an opportunity and has maintained a disciplined capital approach, using post-IPO proceeds to virtually eliminate net debt. Credibility is being tested by persistent GAAP losses, but the team’s focus on adjusted cash metrics and the broker-flagged valuation disconnect suggest confidence in the operational trajectory.",
