        "snippet": "Earnings call transcript: PPHC Q1 2026 sees revenue surge but EPS falls short By Investing.com\n\n# Earnings call transcript: PPHC Q1 2026 sees revenue surge but EPS falls short\n\nInvesting.com\n\nPublished Dec 31, 0000 07:00PM ET\n\nUpdated May 26, 2026 10:04AM ET\n\nPPHC reported a strong revenue performance for the first quarter of 2026, achieving $50.1 million, a 27.5% increase compared to the previous year. Despite this growth, the company’s GAAP earnings per share (EPS) were negative at -0.49, influenced by non-cash charges. The adjusted EPS, however, was positive at $0.25, showing a significant improvement from the previous year. The stock reacted negatively, dropping 5.18% to $870 following the earnings announcement, as investors weighed the financial results.\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n- Revenue increased by 27.5% year-over-year, reaching $50.1 million.\n- Adjusted EPS improved by 75% to $0.25, while GAAP EPS was negative due to non-cash charges.\n- The stock price fell by 5.18% post-earnings bu",
